# Carbon UI and Figma (Balance)

## Stack

- Use `@carbon/react` and `@carbon/icons-react` for UI. Use Carbon Charts when the task needs charts.
- Do not invent custom buttons, inputs, tables, modals, or other primitives when Carbon covers the need.
- Styles: SCSS Modules + `@use '@carbon/react'` (or targeted `@use '@carbon/react/scss/...'`).
- Theme: Carbon-compatible `light` / `dark` / `system`.
- Layout: **mobile-first** — design and implement for the smallest viewport first, then enhance for larger breakpoints (Figma frames and CSS).
- Map Figma designs to `@carbon/react` components — not generic HTML/CSS from Figma autogen, Material, or SDS.

## Canonical Figma file

Work only in this file (`fileKey`: `AKrrn2Cphz7chTu1GwvYTc`):

https://www.figma.com/design/AKrrn2Cphz7chTu1GwvYTc/Balance--Carbon-Design-?node-id=58-2763&p=f&t=fcmZraDygkirkApE-0

This is a Free-plan single-file copy of (v11) Carbon Design System (Community). Team libraries / Enable library across files are unavailable — do not rely on a separate product file or library subscribe.

- App screens live only on pages named `Balance / …` (e.g. `Balance / Screens`). Create that page if missing.
- Do not edit Carbon kit documentation pages (Button, Data table, Tokens, etc.) — read components from them only.
- Build UI from **local** Carbon `COMPONENT` / `COMPONENT_SET` instances in this file.
- Frame names: `Balance / <ScreenName>`.
- Ignore any other Balance Figma file (e.g. empty product file without the kit).

## Design-first gate (required)

When the task **designs a new page/screen** or **adds/changes UI content** on a page (layout, components, copy blocks, navigation, etc.):

1. First implement or update the mockup in the canonical Figma file (Carbon instances on `Balance / *`).
2. Show the user the result (link to the frame/page + short description) and **explicitly ask for confirmation** that the design is acceptable.
3. **Do not write or change UI code** (`apps/web` and related frontend) until the user confirms (e.g. “ok”, “approved”, “good”).
4. After confirmation, implement code to match the approved mockup with `@carbon/react`.

### Gate does not apply when

- Backend / domain / contracts / sync / schema only
- Bugfix with no visual UI change
- Refactor with no visual change
- User explicitly says code-only / skip Figma
